{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.HadronicMass.nucleon_borromean_topology","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.nucleon_borromean_topology","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HadronicMass.nucleon_borromean_topology","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HadronicMass.nucleon_borromean_topology","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HadronicMass/nucleon_borromean_topology.lean#L35-L54","doc":"**Nucleon Borromean topology / Hopf-link binding**\n([`lem:nucleon-borromean-topology`]).\n\nThe proton and neutron are each a Borromean configuration (`6₂³`) of\nthree quark vortices, bound by Hopf links `L_Hopf` (color exchange).\nThe Hopf link is a torus link, so `Vol(L_Hopf) = 0` (`h_vol_hopf`); its\nvolume mass term `mass_volume = Vol_Hopf · c` then vanishes, and the\ntotal mass `mass_total = mass_volume + mass_skein` collapses to the\nSkein mass.  Both numerical clauses are *derived* from the geometric\nhypotheses, not projected. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:nucleon-borromean-topology","label":"lem:nucleon-borromean-topology","md":"quantum-observable-universe/observations/nucleon-borromean-topology.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}